course: dictionary
lesson: 5281
title: Juice and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Juice is the liquid that comes out of fruit or vegetables, like orange juice or apple juice. It can also mean a drink made from that liquid, or a liquid in the body that helps digest food, like stomach juices. Context tells you which one is meant.
explain: «Butterflies drink nectar, fruit juice and water» is about a drink. «Acid such as lemon or lime juice unfolds proteins» is about the liquid from a fruit, used in science. Ask yourself: is this a drink, a liquid from fruit, or a liquid inside the body?
explain: Juice can also be counted or measured. A box or bottle of juice is one item, and juice can be measured in litres, cups or glasses. The words around it show you which sense is in use.
fact: Juice is the liquid that comes out of fruit or vegetables.
fact: Stomach juices are liquids in the body that help to digest food.
fact: Lime juice is an acid, and it can change fish so it turns white even though it has not been heated.
fact: «Searing» means cooking the outside of meat fast on a very hot pan until it is brown. Seared meat does not keep more juices in; it loses as much moisture as unseared meat, but browning adds flavour.
fact: Juice has lots of sugar, so water is better for your teeth.
exercise: «I poured a glass of juice at breakfast.» What is juice here? | A bottle cap | A piece of fruit | *A drink made from fruit liquid | A jar of jam
exercise: «Stomach juices help to digest the food.» What are stomach juices? | Sweet fruit drinks | Pieces of cooked meat | Lemon sweets | *Liquids in the body that help digest food
exercise: «Searing meat does not seal in the juices.» What does searing mean? | Washing meat in cold water | *Cooking the outside fast on a very hot pan until brown | Freezing meat very quickly | Cutting meat into thin strips
test: Juice has lots of sugar, so which is better for your teeth? | Juice | *Water | Juice boxes | Orange juice
test: «Acid such as lemon or lime juice unfolds proteins.» What is lime juice in this sentence? | A type of tree | A kind of meat | *An acid | A sweet dessert
exam: Which meaning of juice is in «Butterflies drink nectar, fruit juice and water»? | A kind of sweet | *Liquid from fruit, used as a drink | Juice that comes out of cooked meat | Liquid in the body that digests food
